# Run Prettier After Changes

After editing or creating any source file, run Prettier on the changed file(s) before finishing the task.

## When to Run

- After using Write, StrReplace, or EditNotebook on code files
- Before marking a task complete or responding to the user
- Skip for markdown-only docs unless the user asked to format them

## How to Run

Format only the files you changed:

```bash
npx prettier --write path/to/changed-file.tsx
```

For multiple changed files in one step:

```bash
npx prettier --write path/to/file-a.tsx path/to/file-b.ts
```

To format the whole project (only when the user asks or many files changed):

```bash
npm run format
```

## Rules

1. Always run Prettier as the last step after code edits — do not skip this.
2. Prefer formatting only changed files over formatting the entire repo.
3. If Prettier fails, fix the issue or report it — do not leave unformatted code.
4. Do not manually reformat to match Prettier; let Prettier apply the project's config.
